data 319
### decision amounts-are-cents
An amount is a whole number of cents, read from text with at most two decimals and written with exactly two.
Why: Sums are compared exactly, as the budget warnings the owner plans need, and a sum of floats cannot be (0.10 and
0.20 do not make 0.30); cents need no dependency (Article 3).

